**Describe the feature**
Regular, bold and italic text styles are used frequently within our slides. Sometimes only one word might be bold (e.g., "Amen."). We would like bold and italic words to stand out in our lower thirds, but bold and italic formatting is lost in a Style's output if "Overrride style with template" is selected. 

**Additional context**
Around line 943 of output.ts, inserting the following right before "text.style = style" appears to resolve this, but it might surprise users expecting previous behavior. 

// preserve bold/italic from original text if the template doesn't explicitly set them
const originalTextStyles = getStyles(text.style)
const templateTextStyles = getStyles(templateText?.style)
if (originalTextStyles["font-weight"] && !templateTextStyles["font-weight"]) {
    style += `font-weight: ${originalTextStyles["font-weight"]};`
}
if (originalTextStyles["font-style"] && !templateTextStyles["font-style"]) {
    style += `font-style: ${originalTextStyles["font-style"]};`
}

